*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*% cups-label-crop-file: label-crop.ppd
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*FileVersion: "1.0"
*LanguageVersion: English
*LanguageEncoding: ISOLatin1
*PCFileName: "LBLCROP.PPD"
*Manufacturer: "cups-label-crop"
*Product: "(Label Crop)"
*ModelName: "cups-label-crop Label Crop"
*ShortNickName: "Label Crop"
*NickName: "cups-label-crop A4/Letter to label"
*PSVersion: "(3010.000) 0"
*LanguageLevel: "3"
*ColorDevice: False
*DefaultColorSpace: Gray
*FileSystem: False
*Throughput: "1"
*LandscapeOrientation: Plus90
*TTRasterizer: Type42
*cupsVersion: 2.0
*cupsModelNumber: 1
*cupsManualCopies: True
*1284DeviceID: "MFG:cups-label-crop;MDL:Label Crop;CMD:PDF;"

*% Accept PDF (and the CUPS pdftopdf output). The filter writes a label-sized PDF
*% as application/vnd.cups-raw, which the labelcrop backend forwards.
*cupsFilter2: "application/vnd.cups-pdf application/vnd.cups-raw 0 label-crop"
*cupsFilter2: "application/pdf application/vnd.cups-raw 0 label-crop"

*% Advertise A4 so iOS AirPrint sends the original A4 or Letter sheet instead of
*% shrinking the whole sheet onto a label-sized page before it reaches CUPS.
*OpenUI *PageSize/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageSize
*DefaultPageSize: A4
*PageSize A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595.28 841.89]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageSize Letter/US Letter: "<</PageSize[612 792]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageSize

*OpenUI *PageRegion/Media Size: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *PageRegion
*DefaultPageRegion: A4
*PageRegion A4/A4: "<</PageSize[595.28 841.89]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*PageRegion Letter/US Letter: "<</PageSize[612 792]/ImagingBBox null>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *PageRegion

*DefaultImageableArea: A4
*ImageableArea A4/A4: "0 0 595.28 841.89"
*ImageableArea Letter/US Letter: "0 0 612 792"
*DefaultPaperDimension: A4
*PaperDimension A4/A4: "595.28 841.89"
*PaperDimension Letter/US Letter: "612 792"

*HWMargins: "0 0 0 0"
*DefaultFont: Courier
*Font Courier: Standard "(1.05)" Standard ROM
